  "dataNotes": "Hole names, pars and Masters yardages follow the 2026 Masters course (7,565 yds; No. 17 Nandina lengthened from 440 to 450 for 2026). Stroke indexes and member-tee yardage (6,365) come from the club's member scorecard as reproduced by Golf Compendium. Augusta National has never had a USGA Course Rating, so both ratings are estimated. Masters tee: 78.1 / 137, the unofficial figure reportedly measured by USGA raters during Masters week (cited by Golf Compendium). Members tee: estimated by taking the length-only scratch rating (about 40.9 + yards/220, so roughly 69.8 for 6,365 yds) and adding the same difficulty premium the Masters-tee estimate carries over its length-only value (about +2.8 for fast, heavily contoured greens and elevation change), giving 72.6; slope 133 is set slightly below the Masters-tee 137. Treat both as approximations.",
